  "description": "Contradiction schematic: parallel horizontal solid representatives a/b/c and separately angled dashed branches crossing at P depict the rejected hypothesis that a meets b at P. Turns and solid/dash distinctions are source facts. The visible modern annotation identifies the dashed/P construction as schematic, not straight extensions. Assertions check the true solid parallel premises and conclusion, depicted dash incidences, and all five stroke endpoints; the rejected hypothesis is not an actual Euclidean relationship to execute.",
